WEBVTT

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.900
<b>Book 3: Revolution to Change the World</b>

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:38.720
Did you kill them?

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:41.490
<b>Episode 11: Confidential File 701, Past and Future</b>

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.490
You must've found Tsukishiro's parting gift.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.820
My family... The entire Karasumori village?

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.250
I did.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:51.970
You've been lying to me this entire time?

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:55.400
Lying to me... for Yoshinobu Tokugawa's sake...

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:59.360
The man who had my clan killed...

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.260
You had me <i>protecting</i> him?

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.510
That's right.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:06.730
I don't understand. Not a single thing.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.330
Nothing you've done makes sense!

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.720
That's an intruder alarm.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.240
The army's special forces 
are headed this way.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.090
Yoshinobu is the only other person 
who knows about this place.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:24.240
He's probably sent them to retrieve you.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.700
He can send whoever he 
likes. It won't stop me!

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.480
You are going to—

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.690
You can kill me now, 
and then you'll be captured

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:37.430
and tapped for your blood until you die.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:42.060
And the blood of the Karasumori will 
continue to be used like a weapon.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.890
At 24:00, be waiting at Shinobazu Pond.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.110
We're here for the Karasumori girl.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:08.830
She's not here.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:10.830
Tell us where she is, then.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.120
I don't know.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:15.810
Maybe he'll feel more talkative 
with a missing arm.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.430
Don't bother.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.180
Sir—

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.810
Can't you tell?

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.890
Torture won't get us anywhere with him.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.140
An underground pathway...

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.640
I'll have another squad mobilized.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.020
She won't be able to escape regardless.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:37.020
Can I assume this means you're 
taking up arms against the shogun?

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.530
I see no reason to answer that question.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.060
I see.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:46.530
Then I may have to kill you 
when next we meet.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.530
Now's your chance! This way!

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:04.910
Hana?!

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.010
Let's get the hell out of here.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:20.660
I seriously can't believe 
you've got me running.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.820
This thing is unwieldy. 
Plus, I run out of breath a lot easier.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.480
Thank you for your help. And...

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.330
What?

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.330
You weren't dead all along.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.330
Sorry to disappoint you.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.390
Told you I could smell you.

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.710
Rinko-san?

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.630
Orders came straight from 
Yoshinobu-sama himself.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.760
He wants you brought in alive.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:54.850
She's a new executioner?

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:57.580
I got nothing against you.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.710
Hell, I think you're all right.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:00.570
But...

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:04.830
This is all I've got!

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:23.670
Not gonna draw that sword?

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.990
You giving up?

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:28.930
No.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:33.250
If you think you've got 
no other choice here,

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:36.190
then I will respond in kind.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:41.690
Because I went through something 
that I can't simply forget.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.700
You are such a dummy.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.870
You think you can screw with me?!

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.300
Quit making me pop the claws.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.240
It takes a lot out of me.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:15.430
I guess it's a small price to pay 
if I can take you alive, though.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:20.810
I'll come see you every day 
as they suck you dry!

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.280
You're gonna have to use your 
powers if you don't wanna die!

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:00.820
You don't have any other means to attack me.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.790
Let's put an end to this.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:09.240
Don't count me out just yet.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.170
I'm through trying to bring you in alive!

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.500
You don't get to walk away and be happy!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.540
We're dying together!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:46.230
I'm asking you to stop.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:04.410
You don't think leaving her alive 
is gonna be a problem later?

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:08.010
No. There's no need for that.

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:13.860
You've actually changed...

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:18.810
Not that I'm one to talk.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:24.730
<b><i>Morning Dew Used Bookstore</i></b>

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:29.860
Jin Kuzuhara said this place is 
still secret, so we should be fine.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.480
Can we really trust him?

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:37.870
It'd be weird if he let you go just to tell 
them where you're hiding, wouldn't it?

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:44.370
He let me live, too, 
and this is my last errand for him.

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:46.750
I'll finally have paid him back.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:51.340
Ugh, not again...

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:54.310
You've been out of town for a while,

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:57.340
so you probably don't know 
how Tokyo has been lately.

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:00.540
Seems like Ryumyaku is starting to dry up.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:03.180
The insurgents have really 
been putting in work.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:06.230
There have been skirmishes every day.

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:09.330
The Tokugawa regime depends on Ryumyaku.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:12.820
It's what keeps foreign powers from invading.

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:15.070
And now, it's almost gone...

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:18.280
Which means the government 
is set for a fall.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:20.600
Ryumyaku was never intended to be used

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:24.310
for the things the Tokugawa 
have done with it.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:27.360
It was bound to come to this sooner or later.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.800
<i>As of the current hour, the entire 
Tokyo metropolitan area is under curfew.</i>

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.970
<i>The military has been mobilized 
in order to suppress riots.</i>

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:39.650
<i>In accordance with the Special 
Capitol Public Order Act,</i>

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:42.440
<i>all individuals seen outdoors 
will be considered rioters,</i>

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:43.970
<i>with orders to shoot on sight...</i>

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:46.640
Looks like the radio station's 
about out of power, too.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:49.830
So, what're you gonna do?

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.150
I...

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:56.610
If you want to go after Jin 
Kuzuhara, you're free to do so.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:00.810
But does it really matter at this point?

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:05.000
If you keep taking everything so seriously, 
you'll be an old lady in no time.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:09.190
Who cares what becomes of the world? 
You should live the way you want.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:13.840
As long as the things you care about are 
safe, what difference does it make?

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.350
Oh, welcome home...

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:27.850
Onee-chan.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:32.610
I heard you were coming back, 
so I thought I should make dinner.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.590
Not many places were open, though.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:37.990
This was all I could buy.

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:40.570
Asahi...

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:43.660
Jin Kuzuhara saved her, apparently.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:47.710
Extorted a med school dropout and self-declared
 revolutionary named Todoroki to do it.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:54.920
Good news, right?

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:59.500
I'm gonna head home. I'd hate to 
put a damper on the big reunion.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.020
Ow, ow, ow...

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:06.010
What's wrong?

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.000
I think the baby is coming...

00:11:23.810 --> 00:11:26.540
The nearest midwife has evacuated.

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:29.950
You're gonna have to do it, then.

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:31.220
But I...

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:38.170
Look... I'm counting on you!

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.410
U-Understood!

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:46.360
Wait, what the hell are you doing?

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:50.230
We have a book on obstetrics, so I thought I'd—

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:50.580
Who gives a shit?!

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:54.010
Boil some water and get 
some towels or something!

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:54.920
All right!

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:56.610
I'll help, too!

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.000
Go!

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:17.930
What is it?!

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:19.140
I can see something!

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:21.150
What the hell is "something"?!

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:23.470
I think it's the baby's head!

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:30.470
Come on! You can do it!

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:56.340
She's here!

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:07.680
Congratulations.

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:09.920
You did a good job, too.

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:17.150
Thank you, Asahi.

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:21.580
She's sleeping soundly.

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:25.070
Whoever heard of having 
a battle for a lullaby?

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:28.150
This little girl has nerves of steel.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:30.660
She must get it from you.

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:32.140
You think so?

00:13:41.990 --> 00:13:43.580
Her hands are so little...

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.970
But warm.

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:50.470
She's warm because she's alive.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:51.760
Yeah.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.720
You're warm, too, Asahi.

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:02.670
I'm so glad that you're alive.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:08.490
I didn't think I'd ever see you again.

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:13.480
I knew I would see you again, Onee-chan.

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.680
Oh, I shouldn't...

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:22.400
I know you'll worry if I cry.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:25.240
So I was trying to hold it in...

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:40.730
I don't want to be apart again.

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:44.140
Please stay with me!

00:14:44.140 --> 00:14:45.140
Okay.

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:47.030
Really?

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:05.850
Thank you.

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.930
Huh? It's chipped...

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:18.560
Let's buy a replacement tomorrow.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:24.390
It really is true...

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:30.050
You're really going to stay here 
from now on, aren't you?

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:32.130
Yes, that's right.

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:33.450
I'm so glad!

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:40.770
That was scary, huh?

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:46.210
I've never helped with a child 
being born before, either.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:51.850
I wonder if that's how hard my mom 
worked to give birth to me.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:57.890
I'm sorry.

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:04.160
In that case, you can teach me.

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:09.540
I can't. I don't know what it was like 
when you were born, Asahi.

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:13.490
Not that! I mean all the things 
a mom teaches her kid.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:17.610
How to hold chopsticks, 
how to cut vegetables,

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:20.930
how to wash the dishes, how to take a bath...

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:23.500
You taught me all that.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:26.220
So you can teach me a bunch more!

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:28.820
I suppose so.

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:36.220
But I don't know all the things a 
parent should teach their daughter.

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:38.840
So...

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:42.190
We'll figure it out together.

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:45.220
Yeah!

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:53.380
I've been meaning to give you these.

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:54.740
What are they?

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.480
Things for schoolwork. They're yours now.

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:58.690
Why?

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:03.370
I've never been to school, or studied.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:05.920
I can do the same, then.

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:13.390
I want you to be able to live a 
different life than I have, Asahi.

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:21.140
Future

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:18.590
Future...

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:21.140
Right. Future.

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:26.470
Tomorrow and beyond. 
All of the time that is ahead of us.

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:30.410
What's ahead of us...

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:33.470
I've been avoiding this 
word for a long time.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:35.150
But...

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:40.100
I think this word is a 
perfect fit for you, Asahi.

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:48.020
In the near future, if you 
haven't had any schooling at all,

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:51.420
it'll be hard to find anyone to marry you.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.680
I don't wanna get married, anyway!

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:57.410
Then you'll definitely need to study, 
or you won't be able to survive.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.370
I guess...

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:01.800
Okay, I'll do it!

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.680
Thank you, Onee-chan!

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:06.680
There's also this...

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:13.020
That's the book you're 
always carrying with you.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:20.420
My mother intended to use this as a diary...

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:24.510
But she died before she 
was able to write in it.

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:32.130
Starting tomorrow, 
let's take turns writing in it.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:34.600
You'll be first, Asahi.

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:36.630
Yeah! I will!

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:38.190
I'd love to.

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:44.230
The day after that will be me, 
and then you again.

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:46.720
We're going to write in it from now on, huh?

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:47.900
That's right.

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:54.190
Starting tomorrow, I'm gonna read books, 
study, write in the diary...

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:57.900
I'll have to cook, too. And do the laundry.

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:01.160
I'm gonna be really busy!

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:05.090
And I'll have to air out the futons...

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:09.860
Do the laundry... 
and look after the store...

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:13.260
I wanna get good at it all...

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:22.160
All of it... together...

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:25.360
With Onee-chan...

00:19:27.570 --> 00:19:29.130
From now on...

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:53.940
<i>Onee-chan!</i>

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:54.770
<i>Which do you want?</i>

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:55.870
<i>Are you gonna kill it?</i>

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:58.150
<i>I'm always trying to kill you, too.</i>

00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:57.750
<i>So, Onee-chan, die.</i>

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:00.110
<i>You died, and were reborn.</i>

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:02.190
<i>You're cute when you laugh.</i>

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:03.980
<i>You're going to live with me!</i>
